  "7521156683230859264": {
   "created": 1793183489,
   "author": "The Content House",
   "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/the-content-house-in_thecontenthousedispatch-activity-7521156683230859264-rZzC",
   "text": "Global AI infrastructure: Investment is rising, but the economics are under pressure.\n\nAI companies are spending heavily on computing infrastructure, even as questions grow over whether the revenue generated will justify the investment.\nTwo recent reports from Gartner and PitchBook show where the market is heading.\n\n1/ Gartner forecasts $6 trillion in AI infrastructure spending between 2027 and 2030.\n\nBut the research firm estimates that AI revenue attributable to data centres will reach only $3.6 trillion through 2030, against $8.5 trillion required to deliver a 12% return on cumulative investment.\n\nMore than $3.5 trillion of infrastructure spending could be exposed to impairment risk by 20",
   "disc_score": 3,
   "checks": {},
   "promoted": false,
   "miss": 0,
   "added": 1793202719
  },
  "7521216502599995392": {
   "created": 1793197751,
   "author": "Inspired Capital",
   "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/inspired-capital-partners_growing-companies-think-their-biggest-problem-activity-7521216502599995392-CXIv",
   "text": "Onboarding is one of the biggest bottlenecks for fast-growing teams. Windmill just launched Agentic Onboarding to fix that. Windy, their AI agent, guides every new hire from day one with a personalized plan, company knowledge, and the right manager support, all in Slack. New hires onboarded with Windmill ramp 3x faster.\n\nWindmill already has a fast-growing roster of customers, like Etched, that are seeing incredible results. Congrats Brian Distelburger, Max Shaw, Mark Tanner and the Windmill team on the launch!",
   "disc_score": 2,
   "checks": {},
   "promoted": false,
   "miss": 0,
   "added": 1793202719
  },
  "7521264448121233408": {
   "created": 1793209182,
   "author": "Index Ventures",
   "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/index-ventures_congratulations-again-to-benjamin-s-and-activity-7521264448121233408-GJOf",
   "text": "Congratulations again to Benjamin S. and the whole team at Flapping Airplanes on their $1B Series A.\n\nFresh off the announcement, our partner Mark Xu sat down with Ben, Flappy\u2019s CEO and co-founder. They talked about everything from his running the student incubator Prod, where he saw startups like Cursor, Mercor, Etched, and dozens of others up close, to building a research lab with a mission to make AI orders of magnitude more efficient. They also get into what Ben believes separates founders from everyone else, and the values he\u2019s bringing to the team: staying focused on fundamentals in an ecosystem full of distractions, and holding their research to the strongest baselines they can come u",
   "disc_score": 46,
   "checks": {},
   "promoted": false,
   "miss": 0,
   "added": 1793220817
  },
  "7521281448989999104": {
   "created": 1793213236,
   "author": "Jared Cohen",
   "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/cohenjar_i-dont-know-anyone-who-thinks-their-company-activity-7521281448989999104-ZBh_",
   "text": "I don\u2019t know anyone who thinks their company does a particularly great job at onboarding new hires. It\u2019s one of the most overlooked parts of building a successful company and usually one of the highest-leverage things to improve upon.\n\nIt is honestly insane that people don't spend more time getting this right given onboarding sets the tone for someone\u2019s entire trajectory within the business. How fast a new hire gets productive, whether they become a top performer, and whether they feel supported while doing so can all be traced back to these early weeks. \n\nToday we\u2019re announcing the system that finally allows companies to launch new hires out of a cannon with repeatable and measurable succes",
   "disc_score": 31,
   "checks": {},
   "promoted": false,
